  "narration_beats": [
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_001",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_000",
      "text": "By the end of this video, you'll have the Orders table open in DB Browser for SQLite, with every row visible on screen.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 23,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_002",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_000",
      "text": "A database table is like a spreadsheet: it stores information in rows and columns, where each row is one record and each column is one type of detail. Understanding this layout is the first step to reading any data in the Orders file.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 43,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_003",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_001",
      "text": "First, click the 'Browse Data' tab at the top of the DB Browser window. This is the view built specifically for looking at table contents, so it's where you'll spend most of your time inspecting real records.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 37,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_004",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_002",
      "text": "Now open the table selector dropdown and choose 'Orders.' This tells DB Browser exactly which table's rows and columns you want to load, since a database file can hold many tables at once.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 33,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_005",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_003",
      "text": "Select the Orders table from the list. This is the object that actually holds every order record, like a stack of receipts organized into neat columns for date, amount, and customer.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 31,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_006",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_004",
      "text": "Give it a moment to load. DB Browser is pulling every row from the Orders table so you can see the full picture, not just a preview.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 27,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_007",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_004",
      "text": "Look at the bottom-left corner of the window: it reads 'Total rows: 128.' That number is your proof the table loaded completely and gives you a fixed count to check against later.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 32,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_008",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_004",
      "text": "You've just opened the Orders table and confirmed all 128 rows are visible, giving you a reliable starting point every time you need to check an order in this database.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 30,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    }
  ],
